WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.665
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:08.317
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.617 --> 00:00:14.752
Unit seventeen: City and Countryside. In this unit, you will compare life in the city and the countryside.

4
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.635
City.

5
00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:19.602
City means a very big and busy town.

6
00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:21.599
Phnom Penh is a big city.

7
00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:24.267
Your turn. Say: City.

8
00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:27.863
City.

9
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:29.898
Countryside.

10
00:00:30.598 --> 00:00:34.246
Countryside means land outside towns with farms and fields.

11
00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:36.882
My grandparents live in the countryside.

12
00:00:37.582 --> 00:00:40.269
Your turn. Say: Countryside.

13
00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:44.017
Countryside.

14
00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:45.913
Busier.

15
00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.172
Busier means more busy.

16
00:00:48.472 --> 00:00:50.564
The city is busier than my village.

17
00:00:51.264 --> 00:00:53.696
Your turn. Say: Busier.

18
00:00:56.396 --> 00:00:57.316
Busier.

19
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.167
Quieter.

20
00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:01.448
Quieter means more quiet.

21
00:01:01.748 --> 00:01:03.760
The countryside is quieter at night.

22
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.984
Your turn. Say: Quieter.

23
00:01:09.684 --> 00:01:10.592
Quieter.

24
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:12.399
Cleaner.

25
00:01:13.099 --> 00:01:14.506
Cleaner means more clean.

26
00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:16.655
The air is cleaner in the countryside.

27
00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:19.531
Your turn. Say: Cleaner.

28
00:01:22.231 --> 00:01:22.907
Cleaner.

29
00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.127
More expensive.

30
00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:28.372
More expensive means costing more money.

31
00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:30.637
Food is more expensive in the city.

32
00:01:31.337 --> 00:01:34.604
Your turn. Say: More expensive.

33
00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:38.630
More expensive.

34
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:40.525
Traffic.

35
00:01:41.225 --> 00:01:43.805
Traffic means the cars and motorbikes on the road.

36
00:01:44.105 --> 00:01:46.058
There is a lot of traffic in the city.

37
00:01:46.758 --> 00:01:49.445
Your turn. Say: Traffic.

38
00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:52.961
Traffic.

39
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:54.754
Compare.

40
00:01:55.454 --> 00:01:58.649
Compare means to look at how two things are the same or different.

41
00:01:58.949 --> 00:02:01.192
Let's compare the city and the countryside.

42
00:02:01.892 --> 00:02:04.069
Your turn. Say: Compare.

43
00:02:06.769 --> 00:02:07.689
Compare.

44
00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:10.753
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.053 --> 00:02:14.364
Sreypich, would you prefer to live in the city or the countryside?

46
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.279
The countryside. It's quieter and cleaner.

47
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.641
But the city is more exciting, isn't it?

48
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.391
Yes, but it's busier and more expensive.

49
00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:28.044
What about traffic?

50
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.547
There's much more traffic in the city!

51
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.697
Grammar focus: Comparatives (-er and more).

52
00:02:35.997 --> 00:02:39.067
The city is busier. The countryside is quieter.

53
00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:44.525
If an adjective ends in -y, change y to i and add -er: busy → busier.

54
00:02:45.517 --> 00:02:48.192
Now read and listen. Two Different Worlds.

55
00:02:48.492 --> 00:02:52.117
I live in the city, but my grandparents live in the countryside.

56
00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:56.496
The city is busier and more expensive than the countryside.

57
00:02:57.783 --> 00:02:59.969
There is more traffic and noise in the city.

58
00:03:01.283 --> 00:03:04.212
The countryside is quieter, and the air is cleaner.

59
00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:08.410
Both places are special, and I love them in different ways.

60
00:03:09.717 --> 00:03:12.079
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:14.204
The city is blank than the village.

62
00:03:14.504 --> 00:03:17.832
A, busier. B, busyer. C, more busy.

63
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:23.851
The answer is A: busier.

64
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.431
Food in the city is blank expensive.

65
00:03:27.731 --> 00:03:30.583
A, more. B, most. C, much.

66
00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:36.908
The answer is A: more.

67
00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:41.043
To look at how two things are different is to blank.

68
00:03:41.343 --> 00:03:44.625
A, compare. B, traffic. C, clean.

69
00:03:48.617 --> 00:03:50.744
The answer is A: compare.

70
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:57.108
Now it's your turn to speak. Would you prefer to live in the city or the countryside?

71
00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:06.242
I would prefer the countryside because it is quieter and cleaner than the city.

72
00:04:06.542 --> 00:04:08.263
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.377
Great work today! You learned eight new words and comparatives (-er and more).

74
00:04:13.677 --> 00:04:19.174
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

75
00:04:19.474 --> 00:04:22.254
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:22.554 --> 00:04:25.113
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

